#: ../../../prop_tgt/PCH_WARNINGS.rst:2
msgid "PCH_WARNINGS"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../prop_tgt/PCH_WARNINGS.rst:6
msgid ""
"Enable compiler warnings for the headers listed in :prop_tgt:"
"`PRECOMPILE_HEADERS`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../prop_tgt/PCH_WARNINGS.rst:8
msgid ""
"By default CMake marks the generated precompiled header file as a system "
"header, which suppresses the diagnostics of every header it includes.  This "
"means that enabling precompiled headers silently hides warnings that the "
"same build would produce without them."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../prop_tgt/PCH_WARNINGS.rst:13
msgid ""
"Set this property to true to omit the system header marker so that the "
"headers collected into the precompiled header are diagnosed as they would be "
"in a build without precompiled headers.  The diagnostics are reported once, "
"while compiling the precompiled header itself, rather than once per source "
"file."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../prop_tgt/PCH_WARNINGS.rst:18
msgid ""
"This property is initialized by the value of the :variable:"
"`CMAKE_PCH_WARNINGS` variable when the target is created."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../prop_tgt/PCH_WARNINGS.rst:21
msgid ""
"The :generator:`Xcode` generator never adds the system header marker, so "
"this property has no effect there."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../prop_tgt/PCH_WARNINGS.rst:24
msgid ""
"Targets that reuse a precompiled header through :prop_tgt:"
"`PRECOMPILE_HEADERS_REUSE_FROM` do not generate a precompiled header of "
"their own, so this property has no effect on them either.  Set it on the "
"target named by :prop_tgt:`PRECOMPILE_HEADERS_REUSE_FROM` instead."
msgstr ""
